Haakon Studebaker wrote:
> I've been playing NetHack the past weekend and noticed something.
> 
> Teleport scrolls nearly always end up being XIXAXA XOXAXA XUXAXA.

I had a brief look into the source code; it seems that in my OS port
there is a initialization of the random number generator before any
object shuffling is done. There are also advanced random functions
implemented, but they are depending on preprocessor tags that may or
may not be active on your system.

In case they are inactive in your environment (and some bad library
handling of random numbers are active on your OS) your observation
would at least be somewhat explainable since object shuffling is one
of the first random tasks to be performed by the game.

> The first runed dagger that I find always ends up in slot "r".

That depends on your option settings; in my configuration the slots
are starting from 'a' and are allocated sequentially, any new item
gets the next available slot starting after the previous allocated
slot. Whenever you drop an item and pick it up again it will land
in the same slot if the slot has not been occipied in the meantime.
Your options setting may vary.

> Coincidence? Groundhog Day effect? Reductive reasoning?

In former times I had the impression that even dungeon maps are
non-random from time to time. In my current Linux environment I
cannot see non-randomness any more with the current NH version.
So I'd guess it's coincidence.

